============================================================ AE. QUICK
CHANGE GUIDE
============================================================

For a new JUnit question: 1. Write the required Java class and method.
2. Create a separate Test class. 3. Add @Test methods. 4. Create an
object of the class. 5. Call the method and verify using
assertEquals/assertTrue/assertFalse. 6. Add invalid/boundary test cases
if needed.

For a new Selenium question: 1. Change driver.get(“URL”). 2. Inspect the
page and change By locator. 3. Change sendKeys(“INPUT”). 4. Use click()
or Keys.ENTER. 5. Wait for the result element. 6. Print getText(),
getTitle(), getCurrentUrl() or getAttribute(). 7. Always close with
driver.quit() in finally.

IMPORTANT: - JUnit examples use JUnit 4 imports and syntax. - Selenium
examples use Selenium 4 and Java. - Selenium website locators are
examples and may need updating after Inspect. - For Chrome, use the
Selenium setup configured in your college lab. - For portal/login
exercises, use only instructor-provided test credentials. - Actual
output and Pass/Fail must be filled after running the program.
